      "content": "Acceptance is a different kind of strength, one that requires immense courage to embrace the finality. If the struggle feels pointless, then finding a quiet, dignified way to meet the inevitable can be an act of profound self-possession. There is grace in choosing how you meet the end, rather than letting the chaos dictate your final moments.",
      "source": "target",
